// 2026-11-01 20:26 CT: more univariate plots (FT-R15, provisional), layout alignment for review (FT-R16), dynamic layouts later (DG-D7).
{"id": "FT-R15", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "More univariate plots, each titled and labelled (FT-R10). Numeric: a histogram with an optional log-scale view for strongly skewed positive values, a box or strip view, and an ECDF. Categorical: a top-N bar chart with an 'other' bucket and the share of rows covered. Text: a string-length histogram. Dates: counts over time at a sensible period, plus day-of-week and month bars. Missingness: a pattern chart showing which columns are missing together on the same rows. Plots appear inline in each column's dictionary entry, not only behind a disclosure, at a size a reviewer can read", "rationale": "Zach 2026-11-01 20:26 CT asked for more univariate plots; the list is claude:aec's proposal, provisional until Zach trims or accepts it", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-6.md", "sha256": "fac7b8cdebc061798d1fd53d0f1a5605fa9da68d99451cbf32b152fac7907046", "locator": "q:I'd like to add more univariate plots, and look at the alignments to better support review.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R16", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "The report's layout supports review: each column's dictionary entry uses the full width, with an aligned statistics table (labels left, numbers right-aligned, thousands separators, sensible rounding and units) beside or above its plots; value/count/share lists are tables, not stacked key/value blocks; raw nested evidence is never the human view (it stays in the JSON and behind a 'raw evidence' disclosure); chart labels sit next to their bars with values at the bar ends; widths and spacing are consistent across sections. The schema sketch no longer reads columns as dates from the word 'time' alone", "rationale": "Zach 2026-11-01 20:26 CT: \"look at the alignments to better support review\". The specifics come from claude:aec's observations of the merged build, listed in the decisions file; they are a reading Zach can correct", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-6.md", "sha256": "fac7b8cdebc061798d1fd53d0f1a5605fa9da68d99451cbf32b152fac7907046", "locator": "q:I'd like to add more univariate plots, and look at the alignments to better support review.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "DG-D7", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "subject": "design", "text": "Report layouts will need more dynamism later (for example responsive or rearrangeable sections, interactive filtering, switchable charts as in FT-R8). Not in the next slice; layouts built now should not block it", "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-6.md", "sha256": "fac7b8cdebc061798d1fd53d0f1a5605fa9da68d99451cbf32b152fac7907046", "locator": "q:Layouts will need to have some better dynamism in the future as well.", "for": "rationale"}]}
// 2026-11-01 23:00 CT: within-group summaries (FT-R7@2), layout-and-formatting review pass (FT-R17).
{"id": "FT-R7", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "When a target (dependent variable) is declared, the report compares the target with each other column using light, type-appropriate measures of association or shared information (for example correlation, correlation ratio, Cramer's V, mutual information, target rates by group or bin), not a fitted model per column; it ranks columns by that relationship and labels every measure as descriptive, not causal. Target-versus-pairs of columns comes later. Model-based comparisons, if any, are opt-in. It also reports within-group summaries: for a grouping column (the target, or a declared or detected category), the count, share and key statistics of other columns within each group (for example the share of traced calls among calls only, or the missing provenance among decisions with status 'proposed'), and flags groups whose pattern differs markedly from the rest, with group sizes shown so small groups are visible", "rationale": "Stated by Zach 2026-11-01 16:55 CT as an addendum to DG-D5. The measures listed are examples; a spec chooses them", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "FT-R7@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:I would also like target-based analyses.", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:I don't want every bivariate comparison to run like a logistic regression", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-2.md", "sha256": "4f7785545588bc80069709a7faf775df9106ca5cb5b593ef48382c403bb7be5a", "locator": "q:and also eventually we'll want target versus bivariate.", "for": "rationale"}, {"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-7.md", "sha256": "4604c4203f1552d449230e5dca19331ebfba17d2b745782a451e13d5c3f08aa9", "locator": "q:Add within-group summaries to the target-analysis requirements.", "for": "rationale"}]}
{"id": "FT-R17", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "acceptance", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Every slice that changes the report gets a layout-and-formatting review pass before it is called done: render the HTML (and any exports it touches) to screenshots at desktop and phone widths, review them visually (image recognition by a capable reviewer), and compare against established practice (data-visualisation and typography conventions, and comparable EDA and profiling reports). The pass lists concrete problems (misalignment, unreadable or unformatted numbers, overflow, crowded or empty regions, unlabelled charts, inconsistent spacing) with screenshots, and either fixes them or records them as open. The builder runs it, and claude:aec runs an independent pass afterwards", "rationale": "Zach 2026-11-01 23:00 CT. Who runs the pass is claude:aec's reading, following the practice of independent review", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "FT-R16@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-A1@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-01-evening-7.md", "sha256": "4604c4203f1552d449230e5dca19331ebfba17d2b745782a451e13d5c3f08aa9", "locator": "q:Also add a pass for layout and formatting, comparing to other artifacts, best practices, or sheer image recognition.", "for": "rationale"}]}
// 2026-11-02 11:16 CT: slice-4 polish (FT-R18).
{"id": "FT-R18", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Report polish after slice 4: (1) cut report length by laying out each column entry as a grid (statistics beside plots) and/or collapsing column entries by default with a compact header line; charts scale to the available width; (2) axes carry intermediate ticks with formatted labels; (3) skewed positive-valued columns with zeros get a log view of the positive values, with zeros counted separately; (4) box-plot annotations never overlap; (5) axis titles are never clipped, on desktop or phone; (6) statistics tables use a logical order (rows, valid, missing; min, quartiles, median, mean, max; spread; zeros, negatives), compact width, rounding appropriate to magnitude and units, and formatted example values; (7) month names capitalised; no top-N chart for identifier-like or near-unique columns (say values rarely repeat instead); the PowerPoint offers a summary deck (a dozen or so slides) by default, with the full deck optional. Each item has a fixture or screenshot check, and the FT-R17 pass is repeated", "rationale": "Zach 2026-11-02 11:16 CT approved sending the items from claude:aec's independent visual pass on slice 4 (relay-kit-private aec-drift/fathom/visual-pass-slice4-2026-11-02.md)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "FT-R16@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "FT-R17@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/decisions/2026-11-02.md", "sha256": "3ac57871f68c9b129a0f9b13b929452c9162aaa60c36a985746ad9d5448a0709", "locator": "q:\"Send it\"", "for": "rationale"}]}
