{"id": "FT-ROW2-R1", "version": 2, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Implement spec010 row-level and temporal structure observations, each with counts, disclosed rule, at most 10 one-based row positions and a paired question, under artifact key row_structure: wholly blank rows and rows blank in every numeric column; positions of exact duplicate rows; repeated-key multiplicity (k rows per column, >=10 keys, k 2..20, >=90% coverage) with within-key constant columns; temporal values outside a >=99% dominant month/year or beyond quartiles +/- 3xIQR; duplicate event timestamps; declared start/end intervals with end<start, end==start and duration distribution in seconds from full ISO date-times, with unparsed pairs counted in the message and raising a question (never shown as a clean 0 of 0); a question only when two temporal columns exist without a declared interval. Temporal outlier rules work at day resolution, so same-day or same-month stragglers are not reported. Never inferred from names, never actions or selection inputs. Proposed for Zach to accept; overlaps open spec-only PR #17 and departs from it in three places (repeat-pattern rather than name-cued keys, >=10 keys rather than >=3, numeric-blank rows rather than year-heading scope), for Zach to reconcile.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RA@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RB@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RE@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RF@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "FT-R14@1"}, {"rel": "supersedes", "to": "FT-ROW2-R1@1"}]}
