{"id": "FT-TS1-R1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Implement spec011 time-series analysis for declared series only (time_series config: time, value or null for event counts, optional by with top-N groups, granularities auto|hour|day|week|month, max_lag): report the observation process (raw rows, distinct and repeated timestamps, missing observations vs explicit zeros vs periods with no event, never merged or imputed); per granularity the four sparsity dimensions in Zach's vocabulary - frequency (zero share, inter-event interval, ADI alias), amplitude (non-zero quantiles, CV2), wavelength (ACF and Durbin-Levinson PACF of values and of the occurrence indicator with 95% bands, dominant and calendar lags, periodogram peak only with the stats extra) and duration (zero-run and burst lengths); reliability notes (n<30 insufficient, constant undefined, lag>n/4 poorly supported); a present/absent/insufficient-evidence signal summary with each rule; questions, not interpretations; artifact key time_series and a report section with ACF/PACF stem plots for two granularities. One question when a temporal and a numeric column exist and nothing is declared. Proposed for Zach to accept; Zach's series-vs-collection question is left open.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RA@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RB@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RC@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RE@1"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "DG-RF@1"}]}
